Karl Garrison wrote:
>
> As I mentioned, this is partially inspired by the initpoly patch,
> which let the player polymorph permanently at game startup into any
> monster form.  Much like this patch, it could be either extremely
> unbalancing or just different and interesting depending on the form
> chosen.

That was my first thought.  It sounded like a variation on being able to
play the game permanently as some monster type.

Python healer with a pet garter snake would be very hard to play without
hands.  Kobold lord with a pet imp would be a very weak start.  Angel
with a pet unicorn could be like getting GDSM from a wish on level one -
So tempting you die in a crowd one level before Medusa.  Maybe even a
Centaur or Dragon with a pet Gnome.


